tumult","H4001":"subjugation","H3998":"confusion","H136":"Lord","H3069":"YHWH/God","H6635":"army","H6979":"to dig","H7023":"wall","H7771":"rich","H413":"to(wards)","H2022":"mount","H5867":"Elam","H5375":"raise","H827":"quiver","H7393":"chariot","H120":"man","H6571":"horse","H7024":"Kir","H6168":"to uncover","H4043":"shield","H1961":"to be","H4005":"best","H6010":"Valley (of Achor)","H4390":"to fill","H7896":"make","H8179":"gate","H1540":"Heglam","H853":"[Obj.]","H4539":"covering","H3063":"Judah","H5027":"to look","H1931":"he/she/it","H5402":"weapon","H1004":"place","H3293":"wood","H1233":"breach","H1732":"David","H7200":"see","H7235":"to multiply","H6908":"to gather","H4325":"water","H1295":"(Shelah) Pool","H8481":"Lower (Beth Horon)","H3389":"Jerusalem","H5608":"to recount","H5422":"to tear","H1219":"to gather/restrain/fortify","H2346":"wall","H4724":"reservoir","H6213":"do","H996":"between","H3465":"(Gate of) Yeshanah","H3335":"formed","H7121":"call to","H4553":"mourning","H7144":"bald spot","H2296":"to gird","H8242":"sackcloth","H2009":"behold","H8342":"rejoicing","H8057":"joy","H2026":"to kill","H1241":"cattle","H7819":"to slaughter","H6629":"flock","H398":"to eat","H1320":"flesh","H8354":"to drink","H3196":"wine","H4279":"tomorrow","H241":"ear","H3068":"LORD","H518":"if","H3722":"to atone","H5771":"crime","H2088":"this","H5704":"till","H3541":"thus","H3212":"to walk","H935":"come","H5532":"be useful","H7644":"Shebna","H834":"which","H6311":"here","H4310":"who?","H2672":"to hew","H6913":"grave","H4791":"height","H2710":"to decree","H5553":"rock","H4908":"tabernacle","H2904":"to cast","H2925":"captivity","H1397":"great man","H5844":"to enwrap","H6801":"to wrap","H6802":"toss","H1754":"circle","H776":"country/planet","H7342":"Broad","H3027":"hand","H8033":"there","H4818":"chariot","H3519":"glory","H7036":"dishonor","H113":"lord","H1920":"to thrust","H4673":"station","H4612":"office","H2040":"to overthrow","H5650":"servant/slave","H471":"Eliakim","H1121":"child","H2518":"Hilkiah","H3847":"to clothe","H3801":"tunic","H73":"girdle","H2388":"strengthen","H4475":"dominion","H5414":"give","H1":"father","H3427":"to dwell","H4668":"key","H7926":"shoulder","H6605":"to open","H369":"nothing","H5462":"to shut","H8628":"to blow","H3489":"peg","H4725":"place","H539":"be faithful","H3678":"throne","H8518":"to hang","H6631":"offspring","H6849":"offshoot","H3627":"article/utensil","H6996":"small","H101":"vessel","H5035":"bag","H5002":"utterance","H4185":"to remove","H1438":"to cut down/off","H5307":"fall","H3772":"cut","H1696":"speak"},"ccc":{},"cccp":{},"com":[["haydock",1,null,"haydock","The valley of vision: Jerusalem. The temple of Jerusalem was built upon Mount Moria, or the mountain of vision. But the city is here called, the valley of vision, either because it was lower than the temple, or because of the low condition to which it was to be reduced, (Challoner) during the captivity. (Worthington) — Vision. Septuagint, “Sion.” (Haydock) — This prophecy regards the devastation caused by Sennacherib, (St. Jerome) Nabuchodonosor, (Sanctius) the Romans, (Eusebius) or by Assaradon, when he took Manasses, 2 Paralipomenon xxxiii. 11., and 4 Kings xxi. 10. — Tops, to weep."],["haydock",2,null,"haydock","Battle. He taxes the king with cowardice."],["haydock",4,null,"haydock","People. He saw this in spirit, though he might not live to witness it. (Calmet)"],["haydock",5,null,"haydock","Searching. That day beheld the Assyrians (Haydock) undermining the wall, and behaving with haughtiness (Calmet) on Mount Sion. (Haydock)"],["haydock",6,null,"haydock","Wall. Arms were frequently hung thereon, Canticle of Canticles ix. 4. (Calmet)"],["haydock",8,null,"haydock","Covering. Hebrew masac, (Haydock) “shade,” for the convenience of the people, 4 Kings xvi. 18. — Forest, built by Solomon. Ezechias has also procured store of arms, which were now delivered out to the citizens."],["haydock",9,null,"haydock","Many, but you have neglected them, (Calmet) till it be too late. (Haydock) — Pool, communicating with Gehon on the west."],["haydock",11,null,"haydock","Walls. Manasses enclosed the pool within walls, forming a second town, 4 Kings xxii. 29. — Ago. You have not imitated the piety of Ezechias."],["haydock",13,null,"jerome","Die. Thus the pagans encouraged themselves to feast. (Calmet) — Ergo vivamus dum licet esse bene. (Petronius) — This conduct betrayed an entire want of faith. (Calmet) — “Nothing offends God so much….as contempt proceeding from despair.” (St. Jerome)"],["haydock",14,null,"haydock","Die. The repentance of Manasses, and the piety of Josias, could not avert the storm. Discite justitiam moniti et non temnere divos."],["haydock",15,null,"haydock","Temple, in the place of Eliacim. He had been secretary before, (Calmet) and had intruded himself into some office in the temple, which he abused. (Worthington)"],["haydock",17,null,"haydock","Cock. St. Jerome’s master assured him that the word which is usually rendered a warrior, has this meaning. (Haydock) — The comparison agrees well with a proud man reduced to misery. (Calmet) — Hebrew, “With the captivity of a man, and he will cover thee.” Septuagint, “he will cast out and bruise the man, and will take away thy comely robe, and throw thee into,” &c. (Haydock)"],["haydock",18,null,"haydock","Lord; Manasses, who hath exalted thee. (Calmet)"],["haydock",20,null,"haydock","Eliacim, who had been displaced, ver. 15. He acted as regent after the departure of Manasses, who always followed his counsels at his return, Judith iv. 5. The priesthood was not then incompatible with civil and military functions."],["haydock",21,null,"haydock","Girdle, the badge of power, Job xii. 18."],["haydock",22,null,"haydock","Shoulder. Here the marks of dignity were worn. Eliacim was appointed master of the palace, over all the other servants. (Calmet) — Thus we may gather what power Christ conferred on St. Peter, when he gave him the keys of heaven, Matthew xvi. 19., and Apocalypse iii. 7. (Haydock)"],["haydock",23,null,"haydock","Peg, on which whatever is placed shall be secure, 1 Esdras ix. 8."],["haydock",24,null,"haydock","House. He shall be the ornament of the priesthood. — Music. All affairs in church and state shall be at his disposal."],["haydock",25,null,"haydock","Fall. Sobna shall lose all his employments, and ruin others. (Calmet)"],["challoner",1,null,"challoner","The valley of vision.... Jerusalem. The temple of Jerusalem was built upon mount Moria, or the mountain of vision. But the city is here called the valley of vision; either because it was lower than the temple, or because of the low condition to which it was to be reduced."]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"],"jerome":["Jerome",1,1,420,"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/#jerome"],"challoner":["Richard Challoner",0,0,1781,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/03566a.htm"]},"fa":[[4,null,0,"Homilies Concerning the Statues","Homily 18",0,407,"Grief is often capable of refreshing distressed souls, and of rendering a burdened conscience light: consider how often women, when they have lost their most beloved children, break their hearts, and perish, if they are forbidden to mourn, and to shed tears. But if they do all which those who are sad, are wont to do, they are relieved, and receive consolation. And what wonder that this should be the case with women, when you may even see a prophet affected in a similar manner? Therefore he was continually saying, \"Suffer me—I will weep bitterly—labour not to comfort me, because of the spoiling of the daughter of my people. …"]],"fau":[["chrysostom","John Chrysostom",1,"father",null,1,407]],"ftr":[["Nicene and Post-Nicene Fathers, series 1, vol. 9 (1889)","https://ccel.org/ccel/schaff/npnf109"]]}